& [Purpose]
  + provide the smallest deterministic user-testable path from ordinary text terms to ordered proof-bearing SemanticAddress matches over the completed lexical sidecar
  + prove the lookup and evidence waist before combining purpose use-case boundary applicability relation or provider behavior
  + make current signed corpus environment artifacts queryable without changing the existing cantor exact query command or exact scanner forms

& [ActivationDecision]
  + activate Slice4B2A lexical lookup request budget term account matched evidence match result fault digest whole-replay forms and one local CLI laboratory
  + activate only lexical token lookup unique-token coverage deterministic ordering complete-union budgets and exact sidecar replay
  + do not activate the broader Slice4B2 semantic query composition purpose use-case boundary authority lifecycle applicability relation pagination cursor or exact-channel suppression behavior
  + preserve AnchorQuery AnchorBudget AssociationContribution AnchorCandidate AnchorQueryResult scan_exact_semantic_anchors and their bytes unchanged

& [RequestAndBudget]
  + LexicalAnchorLookupRequest binds profile request_id ordered original terms and LexicalAnchorLookupBudget
  + terms are the only lexical input and each exact original term receives an account
  + budget binds maximum_terms maximum_query_bytes maximum_unique_tokens maximum_postings maximum_matches and maximum_serialized_result_bytes
  + every numeric bound is positive and capped by compile-time constants
  + duplicate terms and tokens remain observable but do not increase unique-token coverage
  + a term yielding no token remains an explicit term account

& [TermAndEvidenceAccounts]
  + LexicalTermAccount binds original term and exact sorted token-to-occurrence map from cantor-lexical-tokenizer/0.1
  + MatchedLexicalEvidence binds token surface kind surface digest occurrence count and exact evidence_refs copied from one validated posting
  + LexicalAnchorMatch binds one complete exact SemanticAddress sorted unique matched tokens sorted matched evidence and coverage_basis_points
  + repeated token occurrences surfaces aliases and meanings may add evidence but never add unique-token coverage

& [LookupAlgorithm]
  + validate request and whole-replay the supplied DerivedLexicalAssociationIndex against the supplied DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue and same admitted SemanticFabric
  + tokenize each original term and form the sorted unique eligible token union
  + determine the complete number of postings for that union before constructing any match
  + if complete postings exceed maximum_postings refuse LexicalBudgetExceeded without a partial result
  + group every posting by exact unit identity and require one byte-equal SemanticAddress for that identity
  + collect unique matched tokens and exact posting evidence per address
  + compute coverage_basis_points as floor matched_unique_tokens times ten-thousand divided by all eligible_unique_tokens
  + require positive matched count and a value from one through ten-thousand for every emitted match
  + order matches by coverage descending then exact unit package and complete address identity
  + if complete matches exceed maximum_matches refuse without clipping or pagination
  + derive unmatched tokens as eligible tokens absent from all posting evidence

& [ResultAndReplay]
  + LexicalAnchorLookupResult binds result profile request id catalogue fabric index roots tokenizer identity term accounts eligible unmatched tokens complete posting count ordered matches fixed non-authority statement and proof_digest
  + proof_digest commits request complete validated index identity catalogue generation proof result body and exact lookup decision profile under a new domain
  + structural validation recomputes term accounts unique-token coverage match evidence ordering unmatched set budgets and proof digest where possible
  + whole-result validation reruns the complete lookup against request sidecar catalogue and fabric then requires byte equality
  + equal exact inputs serialize byte-identically

& [CLI]
  + add a distinct cantor-anchor-lab binary rather than widening the published cantor query protocol
  + query command accepts --environment one signed EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment JSON and --text one ordinary UTF-8 query surface
  + optional --maximum-postings and --maximum-matches replace conservative defaults within hard caps
  + the CLI preflights and admits every signed environment package then derives a fresh exact catalogue lexical sidecar and lookup result in memory
  + stdout is one closed JSON success envelope binding environment digest result and fixed non-authority statement
  + stderr is one closed JSON fault envelope and a nonzero status
  + no artifact write replacement service provider network or background process occurs

& [AdversarialAcceptance]
  + single and multi-token input repeated terms duplicate token occurrences punctuation non-Latin and empty-token terms are deterministic
  + shared token ambiguity returns multiple ordered exact addresses rather than silently choosing one
  + unique-token coverage ignores repeated occurrences and extra surfaces
  + substring-only matches do not appear
  + missing token remains explicit in unmatched_tokens
  + posting and match budgets refuse before partial response
  + wrong request profile empty terms empty term over-bound bytes tokens postings matches result size coverage order evidence root or proof refuses
  + self-resealed result mutations fail whole replay
  + a tracked signed-corpus CLI fixture produces at least one exact source-bearing match and byte-identical repeated output

& [ProofBoundary]
  + output proves internal deterministic correspondence with admitted signed package bytes catalogue sidecar request and lookup algorithm
  + output does not prove external truth current-world correctness intended-use fitness permission authority safety or instruction validity
  + lexical coverage is relevance evidence only
  + the lab performs no purpose use-case boundary lifecycle authority applicability or relation gate and callers must not infer those gates passed

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty exposes originals tokens occurrences unmatched terms ambiguity coverage arithmetic and the absence of semantic-purpose gates
  + Security admits signed packages validates complete roots enforces finite budgets refuses partial union and gives the lab no write network or effect capability
  + Weaver composes term token posting surface and address associations without inventing synonym or relation edges
  + Planner orders admission catalogue derivation index derivation complete-union accounting aggregation ordering and replay
  + Refiner uses exact unique-token coverage and one small CLI surface without modifying the exact scanner
  + Scribe retains environment catalogue fabric index request surface source evidence result and fault identities
  + Observer requires core positive mutation release CLI repeatability workspace lint format evidence diff and exact scanner hash gates

& [CompletionGate]
  + source manifest SJS activation review and exact phase lock precede code
  + focused core and CLI tests pass in debug and release
  + all twenty-nine completed catalogue and fifteen scanner tests remain green with exact scanner hashes unchanged
